For the default parameters (`WIDTH=8`, `n=16`), these three invariants close the one-step induction: the bound prevents an unreachable index from entering `DONE`, and the other two establish the required count. They also apply when `n >= 0` and `3*n` fits in `WIDTH` bits. Concurrent assertions sample state before the clock edge’s procedural updates. ([accellera.org](https://www.accellera.org/images/resources/videos/SystemVerilog_Assertions_Tutorial_2016.pdf?utm_source=openai))

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (i <= N); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The index starts at zero and increments only while below N. This reachable-state bound rules out an index above N when the FSM enters DONE."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (sum == i / 3); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Each increment of i to a multiple of three also increments sum, so sum tracks the number of such multiples reached."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (state != DONE || i == N); endproperty",
      "explanation": "With lemma_1, the LOOP exit condition can become true only at i == N. In DONE, lemma_2 then gives sum == N / 3 == n."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

For the default parameters, `i` advances from 0 to `N=48`, and `sum` increments at each multiple of 3. The three invariants below jointly make `prop` 1-inductive over reset-reachable states.

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (i <= N); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Bounds the loop index, ruling out unreachable values that would otherwise prevent an inductive proof of the DONE transition."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) ((state != DONE) || (i == N)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The machine enters DONE only after the index reaches N, and the index then remains unchanged."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (sum == i / 3); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Each completed group of three iterations increments sum once. Together with lemma_2 and N=3*n, this establishes sum==n in DONE."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

These lemmas assume reset initialization, nonnegative `n`, and a non-overflowing `N=3*n` that fits in `i`; the default parameters satisfy those conditions.

For the default parameters, the three lemmas below **jointly make `prop` 1-inductive**. They rely on `N = 3*n` fitting in `i`; because `i = i+1` is a blocking assignment, the `% 3` test uses the incremented value. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F23/documentation/1800-2017.pdf#page=1))

